problem:
Problem description
- There is a single-period livestock planning problem for a farm that must decide how many animals of each available type to raise.
- The animal types are collected in the set $$\mathcal{A}$$, indexed by $$a \in \mathcal{A}$$.
- Each animal type $$a$$ has a unit selling price $$s_a$$, a unit feed cost $$f_a$$, and a unit manure output $$g_a$$ over the planning period.
- The farm operates over a planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$ representing the aggregate daily decision window.
- The farm has a manure-handling capacity $$G^{\max}$$ for the planning period.
- Some animal types may have type-specific minimum required quantities $$\underline{x}_a$$ and/or maximum allowed quantities $$\overline{x}_a$$.
- The farm also has an overall livestock capacity $$H^{\max}$$ limiting the total number of animals raised across all types.
- The planning goal is to choose animal quantities that maximize total profit, where profit is defined as total selling revenue minus total feed cost.
- Required business constraints:
  - The total manure generated by all raised animals must not exceed the manure-handling capacity.
  - Each animal type must satisfy its applicable minimum and maximum quantity requirements.
  - The total number of animals raised across all types must not exceed the overall livestock capacity.
  - All chosen animal quantities must be nonnegative integers.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_a$$: the number of animals of type $$a$$ to raise.
  - $$Z^\star$$: the maximum total profit achieved by the selected livestock plan.

Input Format
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
    "description": "Planning horizon for the aggregated livestock decision."
  },
  "sets": {
    "animals": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{A}$$",
      "description": "Set of animal types available for raising, indexed by $$a \\in \\mathcal{A}$$."
    }
  },
  "parameters": {
    "sell_price": {
      "symbol": "$$s_a$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{A}|$$",
      "description": "Unit selling price for each animal type $$a$$."
    },
    "feed_cost": {
      "symbol": "$$f_a$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{A}|$$",
      "description": "Unit feed cost for each animal type $$a$$."
    },
    "manure_rate": {
      "symbol": "$$g_a$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{A}|$$",
      "description": "Unit manure produced by one animal of type $$a$$ over $$\\mathcal{T}$$."
    },
    "manure_capacity": {
      "symbol": "$$G^{\\max}$$",
      "description": "Maximum total manure that can be handled over $$\\mathcal{T}$$."
    },
    "lower_bound": {
      "symbol": "$$\\underline{x}_a$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{A}|$$",
      "description": "Minimum required quantity for animal type $$a$$; use a null or inactive value when no minimum applies."
    },
    "upper_bound": {
      "symbol": "$$\\overline{x}_a$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{A}|$$",
      "description": "Maximum allowed quantity for animal type $$a$$; use a null or inactive value when no upper limit applies."
    },
    "total_capacity": {
      "symbol": "$$H^{\\max}$$",
      "description": "Maximum total number of animals that can be raised across all types."
    }
  },
  "decision_variables": {
    "quantity": {
      "symbol": "$$x_a$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{A}|$$",
      "type": "nonnegative integers",
      "description": "Number of animals of type $$a$$ to raise."
    }
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "solution": {
    "selected_quantity": {
      "symbol": "$$x_a$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{A}|$$",
      "type": "nonnegative integers",
      "description": "Optimal number of animals to raise for each type $$a$$."
    },
    "total_profit": {
      "symbol": "$$Z^\\star$$",
      "type": "real number",
      "description": "Maximum achievable total profit under the given constraints."
    }
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "time_horizon": "one_day",
  "animals": ["cow", "sheep", "chicken"],
  "sell_price": {
    "cow": 500,
    "sheep": 200,
    "chicken": 8
  },
  "feed_cost": {
    "cow": 100,
    "sheep": 80,
    "chicken": 5
  },
  "manure_rate": {
    "cow": 10,
    "sheep": 5,
    "chicken": 3
  },
  "manure_capacity": 800,
  "lower_bound": {
    "cow": 10,
    "sheep": 20
  },
  "upper_bound": {
    "chicken": 50
  },
  "total_capacity": 100
}
